  "source_text": "Hecks.bluebook \"Metering\" do\n  # A CORPUS-OWNED DOMAIN (docs/semantics/bluebook-semantics.md, C4.2).\n  # A command's effects are ONE UPDATE SET evaluated against the\n  # pre-dispatch state: every source reads the state as it was before\n  # the command, whatever order the effects are declared in. `Read`\n  # deliberately declares `sets :current` BEFORE `sets :previous, to:\n  # state(:current)` — under sequential, intermediate-reading effects\n  # (the pre-C4.2 reading of both runtimes) `previous` would copy the\n  # value `current` had JUST been set to; under C4.2 it copies the\n  # reading the meter held before this one. No example domain reads a\n  # field it writes in the same command, so the clause needed its own.\n  vision \"A meter keeps its latest reading and the one before it.\"\n  core\n\n  aggregate \"Gauge\" do\n    identified_by :tag\n\n    attribute :tag,      Tag\n    attribute :current,  Reading, default: { value: 0 }\n    attribute :previous, Reading, default: { value: 0 }\n\n    value_object \"Tag\", String\n\n    value_object \"Reading\", Integer\n\n    command \"Install\" do\n      goal \"Mount a gauge, reading zero\"\n      attribute :tag, Tag\n      emits \"MeterInstalled\"\n    end\n\n    command \"Read\" do\n      goal \"Take a reading, keeping the one before it\"\n      reference_to Gauge\n      attribute :current, Reading\n      # DECLARED WRITE-FIRST ON PURPOSE — see the header.\n      sets :current\n      sets :previous, to: state(:current)\n      emits \"MeterRead\"\n    end\n  end\nend\n"
}